Z||000000||Eric_PA||08-16-2000||10:13 PM||||Hi, I am currently prepairing for a Quad engine swap into my fiero. I have been acquiring the items I need for a little over a year and getting close to the start of a wonderful project. There is one thing that I can't decide on yet. That is how am I going to mount the right side of the engine to the sub frame? I was thinking that maybe I could use some sort of adjustable torque rod with two mounting brackets, one for the engine and one for the sub frame. I was told that the engine would flop around if I do this. Also such a setup would be very rigid. I would really like to use some sort of bushing to absorb vibration a little. Has anyone done this or have pics that would show how to acomplish this? I am thinking about getting the ACE kit to save time, but is that really complete? Looking for any info or ideas on how to mount the Quad on the right side. I allready have trans brackets and a way to mount the front of the engine. I will be using the existing engine mount for the front. <P>Thanks,<BR>Eric<BR>86.5 GT||||reg||5
